1
00:00:01,730 --> 00:00:04,940
The entrance to the brothel is inside this door.

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,980
The actual establishment
extends out underground,

3
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:10,150
and according to the assassin,
there appears to be another entrance

4
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:12,160
in that building over there.

5
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,570
Then how about Climb and I attack there,

6
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:18,830
and you go in through here, Lord Sebas?

7
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:23,290
We can have him contain the entrance,
while I search through the inside.

8
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:24,330
Very well.

9
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:27,460
I have no objections, Lord Unglaus.

10
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:30,420
I wish you'd start calling me Brain.

11
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:33,760
Lord Sebas, I would be pleased
if you would call me that, too.

12
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:34,840
Mm-hmm.

13
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:36,970
All right, let's go.

14
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:37,850
--Right.
--Right.

15
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:39,850
One other thing--

16
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,350
I will take as many prisoners as I can,

17
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:45,350
but if anyone offers resistance,
I will kill them without remorse.

18
00:00:45,690 --> 00:00:47,480
You have no problem with that, yes?

19
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:52,570
Since our numbers are so few,
I think it is unavoidable to some extent.

20
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:56,320
But if anyone who might be
one of Eight Fingers' captains is here,

21
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:59,120
can I ask that you please apprehend them?

22
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,080
I am not a hardened killer.

23
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:06,210
It is not as though I am here
to kill everyone in sight, so rest easy.

24
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,310
Picking locks is not one of my specialties.

25
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:34,030
Wh-What the...?!

26
00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:35,490
Hey, what was that sound?

27
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:45,230
It was rusted, so I had to
force it open just a bit.

28
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:29,270
There's a secret door right there.

29
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:32,230
Wow, that's a pretty handy item.

30
00:03:32,230 --> 00:03:36,360
Yes. A certain lady gave me these
for such a time as this.

31
00:03:36,610 --> 00:03:39,230
It is dangerous to go searching
around without a thief, after all.

32
00:03:44,990 --> 00:03:46,990
Sure enough, it was booby-trapped.

33
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:49,240
A poison arrow.

34
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:53,120
So, what now? I'd like to have you
watch the entrance.

35
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,620
Would you wait here?

36
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:57,130
I'm not very good at indoor combat.

37
00:03:57,420 --> 00:04:00,880
If possible, I'd rather keep to open areas,
where it's easier to fight.

38
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:02,800
Okay, you want to go together?

39
00:04:03,010 --> 00:04:03,930
Yes.

40
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:17,740
Hey, what's the matter?
You through already? Eh?!

41
00:04:23,990 --> 00:04:28,780
Now that I think about it, I liked
the voice of that woman who ran away.

42
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:35,840
Wha--?!

43
00:04:36,710 --> 00:04:39,290
You like hitting, do you?

44
00:04:39,290 --> 00:04:41,340
Y-You!

45
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,680
You hink you can ged away wi--

46
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:57,810
Sdob dat!

47
00:04:57,810 --> 00:04:59,520
Is this wrong?

48
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:03,110
Ob course id is! Who do you hink I ab?!

49
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:05,740
A mere fool.

50
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:09,120
For pity's sake, isn't this an awful sight?

51
00:05:11,370 --> 00:05:12,370
You hool--

52
00:05:14,330 --> 00:05:17,470
Domebody! Id anybody dere?!

53
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:21,670
Why idn'd anybody cobing oud?

54
00:05:21,670 --> 00:05:26,220
Because they are dead,
or they are unconscious.

55
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:28,840
Ib-b-boddible!

56
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:33,220
Now then, I feel no need to spare your life.

57
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:36,100
You are going to die here.

58
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:38,850
W-W-Waid! Why are you doing dis?!

59
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:43,360
You don't know,
even in light of all you've done?

60
00:05:46,030 --> 00:05:47,280
I see.

61
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:51,530
I-I-I can gibe you boney, jusd don'd kill be!

62
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:54,700
This is what it means to be unworthy of life!

63
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:59,650
Stay there and die.

64
00:06:21,770 --> 00:06:25,320
It's a bit noisy. Let's open it.

65
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:31,030
Do you want to wait here?

66
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,030
Yes.

67
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:35,370
Okay, I'm going to go look around inside
and be back right away.

68
00:06:35,370 --> 00:06:37,410
Don't get yourself killed, Climb.

69
00:06:37,410 --> 00:06:39,450
I appreciate it, Lord Ung--

70
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,600
Lord Brain, you be careful, too.

71
00:06:55,350 --> 00:06:56,680
It's empty?

72
00:07:02,730 --> 00:07:04,650
Oh, well, I guess.

73
00:07:06,530 --> 00:07:08,010
And over here...

74
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:12,280
What are these? Spare uniforms?

75
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:21,710
And here we deliberately came
via the hidden passageway,

76
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:25,210
since the alarm alerted us to intruders.

77
00:07:25,210 --> 00:07:28,880
Succulent, it doesn't do
any good mentioning that now.

78
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:31,260
Six Arms...

79
00:07:31,430 --> 00:07:34,090
Oh, I know this boy.

80
00:07:34,090 --> 00:07:37,930
He's the underling of that female
I hate more than anyone in the world!

81
00:07:37,930 --> 00:07:40,020
You mean the princess?

82
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:44,270
I'd like to take the boy
back with us, too. What do you say?

83
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:47,150
I'll have to charge
a separate fee, if you please.

84
00:07:47,150 --> 00:07:48,400
Okay.

85
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:53,780
Please help me!

86
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:59,450
Cocco Doll, it may prove a bit
difficult to take him back with us.

87
00:07:59,450 --> 00:08:02,870
What do you mean?!
You're one of the Six Arms, right?

88
00:08:02,870 --> 00:08:04,420
You're not worthy
of the name "Illusion Demon."

89
00:08:04,710 --> 00:08:05,790
Illusion Demon?

90
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:09,630
I'll have to deal with this
before any reinforcements show up.

91
00:08:09,630 --> 00:08:12,300
Nonetheless, I will try as best I can,

92
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:18,430
but please don't forget that
once you get clean away, we will prevail.

93
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:20,930
I'm going to guard this door with my life!

94
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:25,690
As long as nothing happens to me,
you guys aren't getting away!

95
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:29,940
We'll find out soon enough
whether that's possible.

96
00:08:57,800 --> 00:09:00,220
--What?
--Sorry about that.

97
00:09:00,510 --> 00:09:03,270
I'm going to kill the kid, right here.

98
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:07,480
You can't! He will make for
a fine card to play against that girl!

99
00:09:07,770 --> 00:09:10,150
We've been fed the wrong impression.

100
00:09:10,150 --> 00:09:12,150
If he had friends
on the other side of that door,

101
00:09:12,150 --> 00:09:14,490
we would have been surrounded.

102
00:09:14,650 --> 00:09:15,650
Then...

103
00:09:15,650 --> 00:09:21,620
I am the only escort you have.
For us to get away safely...

104
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,870
...I have to kill him, right now!

105
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:32,880
Is that a Martial Art? A defensive battle
won't work here. Which means...

106
00:09:37,050 --> 00:09:38,300
So that's it!

107
00:09:39,470 --> 00:09:40,050
Hmm?

108
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,640
Your right arm itself is an illusion!

109
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:45,560
Your actual arm and sword
have been turned invisible!

110
00:09:46,890 --> 00:09:47,940
That's right.

111
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:50,560
This is nothing more than magic
that makes part of me invisible

112
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:53,440
combined with magic that creates an illusion.

113
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:57,950
My character classes
are both illusionist and fencer.

114
00:09:57,950 --> 00:10:00,820
It's not a very interesting trick
if you know how it's done, is it?

115
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,700
Feel free to laugh.

116
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:05,330
Seeing as how I divided my abilities,

117
00:10:05,330 --> 00:10:09,330
I may be considered
lower than you as a warrior, per se.

118
00:10:09,630 --> 00:10:15,340
However, are you able
to discriminate illusion from reality?

119
00:10:15,710 --> 00:10:17,460
Multiple Vision.

120
00:10:20,010 --> 00:10:23,760
Martial Art! Ability Boost!
Mental Enhancement!

121
00:10:28,350 --> 00:10:30,600
Scintillating Scotoma.

122
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:35,230
Wrong one!

123
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:36,440
Martial Art! Evasion!

124
00:10:44,030 --> 00:10:44,870
This one!

125
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:49,920
One out of two!

126
00:10:57,210 --> 00:11:03,300
I guess... I can't say I've won yet.
But if I can apprehend Succulent...

127
00:11:06,970 --> 00:11:11,650
Unfortunately for you,
that's not going to happen.

128
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:16,780
Fox Sleep. It's an illusion spell
that activates after being injured.

129
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,650
It hurt, too.

130
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:23,530
I'm afraid we're out of time,
so I'm going to finish the job now.

131
00:11:23,530 --> 00:11:26,290
Listen, are you sure
we can't take him back with us?

132
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:28,660
Give me a break.

133
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:32,790
There's a good chance that this kid's pals
are on the other side of this door.

134
00:11:32,790 --> 00:11:34,520
Please, let it go.

135
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:47,180
I can't... die yet... Not until...

136
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:52,270
I repay the debt... I owe Princess Renner...

137
00:11:56,110 --> 00:11:58,190
I-Impossible!

138
00:11:58,730 --> 00:12:01,530
That should have been a mortal wound!

139
00:12:01,530 --> 00:12:03,660
How can you get back up?!

140
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:06,660
Why won't you die?!

141
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:11,000
Wh-What is this?!

142
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:21,470
Damn it, you use your feet, too?!

143
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:29,850
One last struggle, was it?

144
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,980
You sure gave me a scare.

145
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:34,350
Why don't you stop right there?

146
00:12:40,990 --> 00:12:42,240
Right down to the wire, huh?

147
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:45,910
What are you waiting for?
Hurry up and kill that guy!

148
00:12:45,910 --> 00:12:50,100
If I tried that, he would rush me
and cut me down with a single strike.

149
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:56,250
Climb, are you all right?
Do you have any items that heal wounds?

150
00:12:56,250 --> 00:12:58,250
Yes... I do...

151
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,490
Okay.

152
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:04,630
From here on, you're facing <i>me</i>.

153
00:13:04,970 --> 00:13:07,140
I will exact retribution for him.

154
00:13:07,930 --> 00:13:09,680
May I ask your name?

155
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:12,770
Brain Unglaus.

156
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:15,100
What? You're him?!

157
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:17,650
No way! It's really him?!

158
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:21,940
The old me might have felt pleased by the fact

159
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:25,570
that most of the people
I've met today already knew who I was,

160
00:13:25,570 --> 00:13:27,910
but right now, it's a bit more complicated.

161
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:32,910
Hey, Unglaus,
why don't we call off the fighting?

162
00:13:32,910 --> 00:13:37,330
You are a lot like we are.
Power... is what you desire, right?

163
00:13:37,330 --> 00:13:39,340
I can see it in your eyes.

164
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:43,960
So why don't you join us?
Eight Fingers is the best organization

165
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,680
for those who possess power.

166
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,600
You can obtain powerful magic items!

167
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,720
High-value weapons and protective gear, too!

168
00:13:51,930 --> 00:13:53,310
What tripe.

169
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:56,560
Is that all you people are?

170
00:13:56,730 --> 00:13:57,650
What?!

171
00:13:57,850 --> 00:13:59,520
I'm putting you on notice.

172
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:03,030
Our strength does not amount to much.

173
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,900
Also, there's one thing I've learned--

174
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:10,240
Strength on behalf of someone else
surpasses individual strength.

175
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:16,160
Maybe that's not much, but even so,
it's something I've realized.

176
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:23,130
What a shame, Unglaus.
Imagine, me having to kill a gifted warrior

177
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:25,670
who once fought evenly matched
against even Stronoff!

178
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:31,680
You think you--you, who wield your sword
only for yourself--can do that?

179
00:14:31,890 --> 00:14:35,020
Yeah, I can kill you! I can kill you easily!

180
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:38,690
I'll kill you, then I'll kill
the kid slumped over, there!

181
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:42,900
Please be careful.
Succulent uses illusion techniques.

182
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:45,680
What you see is not necessarily real.

183
00:14:45,990 --> 00:14:49,450
You don't say. That does indeed
make him a tricky opponent...

184
00:14:54,950 --> 00:14:56,200
...but not a problem.

185
00:14:56,950 --> 00:14:58,120
One strike.

186
00:14:58,540 --> 00:14:59,330
What?!

187
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:03,590
I said I would end this
with one strike, Succulent.

188
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,530
Then go ahead and try!

189
00:15:21,310 --> 00:15:25,650
My Field can detect even invisible beings.

190
00:15:25,650 --> 00:15:31,030
You might have been planning to kill Climb,
then claim I couldn't protect him,

191
00:15:31,030 --> 00:15:33,030
but you tried it with the wrong opponent.

192
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:35,160
See? One strike.

193
00:15:37,370 --> 00:15:38,790
Nicely done!

194
00:15:38,790 --> 00:15:40,460
Nicely done.

195
00:15:43,130 --> 00:15:44,880
Wh-When did you get here?

196
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:47,550
Just this moment.

197
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:49,840
Y-You did?

198
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:54,020
I didn't detect him with my Field.

199
00:15:54,850 --> 00:15:58,270
Who exactly is this man, anyway?

200
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:08,480
The women being held prisoner
have been taken into protective custody.

201
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:10,360
Thank you most sincerely!

202
00:16:11,150 --> 00:16:14,280
I must remain here briefly,
for the after-incident report.

203
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,490
What about you two?

204
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:18,870
Oh, I think it's time I took off.

205
00:16:18,870 --> 00:16:21,500
Then I shall take my leave, as well.

206
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:31,630
Welcome back, Lord Sebas.

207
00:16:32,550 --> 00:16:34,010
Lord Sebas,

208
00:16:34,390 --> 00:16:37,640
Lord Ains is waiting for you inside.

209
00:16:48,730 --> 00:16:51,570
Is that you, Climb? Please come in.

210
00:16:56,410 --> 00:16:59,240
Forgive me for being gone so long.

211
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,620
I was worried.

212
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:05,750
I really was worried, you know.

213
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:09,630
So, tell me exactly what happened.

214
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:13,860
I see.

215
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:17,640
Tomorrow, or the day
after tomorrow at the latest,

216
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:20,640
we will be staging attacks
on seven Eight Fingers facilities.

217
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:23,140
With the raid on the brothel today,

218
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:27,270
one can predict that as more time passes,
their security will grow tighter.

219
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:31,400
I'm terribly sorry.
This is all because I went off on my own.

220
00:17:31,650 --> 00:17:33,900
No, please don't let it bother you.

221
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:36,530
We should think of it
as having made our resolve.

222
00:17:36,530 --> 00:17:38,910
We arrested Succulent, one of the Six Arms,

223
00:17:38,910 --> 00:17:42,270
as well as Cocco Doll,
head of their slave trade division.

224
00:17:42,870 --> 00:17:46,830
This will be enough to shake
the very pillars of their organization.

225
00:17:46,830 --> 00:17:51,800
Which is all the more reason why
I want to strike another blow to them.

226
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:56,680
Another blow, before they
leave the kingdom with any information.

227
00:17:58,180 --> 00:17:59,310
As you wish!

228
00:18:00,140 --> 00:18:04,560
I believe tomorrow will be a hectic day.
Please watch yourself.

229
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:06,900
Right!

230
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:13,690
Ho, Climb and that Six Arms man?

231
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:17,360
Yeah. He had been struck a fatal blow,

232
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:20,370
but it looked like he had
Succulent cornered pretty well.

233
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:21,700
Did he?

234
00:18:24,870 --> 00:18:27,670
It's true, he has no talent with the sword.

235
00:18:27,670 --> 00:18:30,040
So much so that when I first saw him,

236
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:32,960
I pegged him as nothing more
than a kid vainly struggling for power.

237
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:36,760
But then, he faced that terror--

238
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:39,890
the kind of bloodlust that rivaled
that monster I ran away from,

239
00:18:39,890 --> 00:18:40,970
and withstood it.

240
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:44,720
In that regard, the boy is better than me.

241
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:47,350
How unbelievable is that?

242
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:50,370
Nope, the world is a big place.

243
00:18:51,110 --> 00:18:54,820
The person that gave Climb
this training is one thing,

244
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:57,360
but this monster you say
you ran into has my attention.

245
00:18:58,070 --> 00:19:00,740
Her name is Shalltear Bloodfallen.

246
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:03,450
I think she's most likely a vampire.

247
00:19:03,450 --> 00:19:07,120
She stopped the technique I came up with,
the one I devised to defeat you,

248
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,370
with just one hand.

249
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:10,870
I see.

250
00:19:11,130 --> 00:19:15,000
Stronoff, if you ever see her,
do not challenge her to battle.

251
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:21,640
I appreciate the warning. But if this
"Shallty" monster is after the king,

252
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:24,640
then I will fight her,
even at the cost of my own life.

253
00:19:25,010 --> 00:19:28,640
That's "Shalltear." Shalltear Bloodfallen.

254
00:19:33,150 --> 00:19:35,730
Hey, don't get any on the food.

255
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:39,360
It might take on the wine's flavor,
and taste pretty good.

256
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:42,240
My sense of taste is shot, so I wouldn't care.

257
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:45,120
Don't tell me yours is, too, Unglaus.

258
00:19:45,490 --> 00:19:46,990
It's Brain.

259
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,250
Call me Brain.

260
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:52,510
Okay, in that case, I'm Gazef.

261
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:55,290
Got it, Gazef.

262
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:03,640
All right,

263
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,260
good night to you.

264
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:06,570
Good night.

265
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:16,900
Now then, the maid on duty tonight is...

266
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,650
Ah yes, it's <i>her</i>.

267
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:25,440
The one who looks like she's made fun of Climb.

268
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:29,540
Let's see, which face was the right one, again?

269
00:20:33,170 --> 00:20:36,570
This is the smile I wear
when receiving others as a princess.

270
00:20:45,930 --> 00:20:48,560
This one is best, isn't it?

271
00:20:56,940 --> 00:20:58,440
You rang for me?

272
00:20:58,730 --> 00:21:02,440
I have a request.
Can you prepare a bath for me?

273
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:05,450
Very good, Princess Renner.

274
00:21:06,870 --> 00:21:08,740
Is something the matter?

275
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:12,330
It's amazing! Climb just performed
an incredible feat!

276
00:21:12,620 --> 00:21:15,040
Then congratulations are in order.

277
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:18,420
You know what?
He put down these terribly bad men!

278
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:21,130
Then he freed some others
who had been held captive.

279
00:21:21,130 --> 00:21:24,970
--They're at a guardhouse somewhere now.
--I'll kill her. I'll kill her, too.

280
00:21:24,970 --> 00:21:29,480
--Is that right?
--If anyone makes fun of my Climb...

281
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:33,480
...I'll kill them.

282
00:22:33,830 --> 00:22:37,240
I'll have to apologize to Cocco Doll, I guess.

283
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:41,460
Despite letting him have Succulent,
one of the Six Arms,

284
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:44,090
this place still fell as easily as it did.

285
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:48,970
So then, Boss, now that Succulent
has been caught, do we kill him?

286
00:22:49,340 --> 00:22:52,350
The man does have his uses.

287
00:22:52,350 --> 00:22:56,100
Reach out to the count and
ask to have him released within the day.

288
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:59,270
So what do we do? Step back?

289
00:22:59,270 --> 00:23:01,650
I doubt that there's enough benefit involved

290
00:23:01,650 --> 00:23:03,610
to justify the losses we'd take
in going up against this.

291
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:08,740
Don't be ridiculous. We have to make
an example of those who hit the brothel,

292
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:11,280
or our reputation will be diminished.

293
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:13,620
Don't even consider losses at this point.

294
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:16,500
Davernoch, the Undead King...

295
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:18,770
Peshurian, of the Spatial Slash...

296
00:23:19,370 --> 00:23:22,250
EdstrÃ¶m, of the Dancing Scimitar...

297
00:23:22,630 --> 00:23:25,130
Malmvist, of the Thousand Kills...

298
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:29,010
As well as myself, Zero, the Battle Demon...

299
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:33,070
We'll show whoever attacked us a hell on earth!

300
00:23:34,390 --> 00:23:38,770
We'll more than make them regret
doing anything this foolish!

301
00:23:38,770 --> 00:23:40,770


